 polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Tom Suozzi (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Tom Suozzi, a Democratic incumbent in a Long Island district Donald Trump carried in 2024, faces a rematch-style challenge from Republican Mike LiPetri. Suozzi has built a commanding financial lead, with $5.7 million on hand compared to LiPetri's $0.7 million, though a Trump-linked super PAC has put $8 million into ads attacking Suozzi over stock trading. Expert raters split between Lean D and Likely D, with two calling it Safe D, and prediction markets price Suozzi's win chances near 88 percent.\n\nThe race remains competitive because of the district's even partisan lean and the national midterm environment, but Suozzi's incumbency, fundraising edge, and cross-party appeal keep him clearly favored. No public general-election polling is available, so the forecast leans on fundamentals, ratings, and market pricing.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9133, "margin": 9.07}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.894, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8981, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.907, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8709, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8973, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8955, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9136, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9155, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9242, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9213, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9012, "margin": 8.5}]}